{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the base \\( b \\) and the digit \\( P \\) such that the multiplication of \\( P_b \\) by \\( P_b \\) results in \\( 31_b \\). We know that \\( P = b - 1 \\).\n\nFirst, let's express \\( P_b \\) and \\( 31_b \\) in base 10. The number \\( P_b \\) in base 10 is \\( P \\), and the number \\( 31_b \\) in base 10 is \\( 3b + 1 \\). Therefore, we have the equation:\n\\[ P \\times P = 3b + 1. \\]\nSince \\( P = b - 1 \\), we substitute \\( P \\) with \\( b - 1 \\):\n\\[ (b - 1)^2 = 3b + 1. \\]\nExpanding and simplifying the equation, we get:\n\\[ b^2 - 2b + 1 = 3b + 1. \\]\nSubtracting 1 from both sides, we have:\n\\[ b^2 - 2b = 3b. \\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[ b^2 - 5b = 0. \\]\nFactoring out \\( b \\), we get:\n\\[ b(b - 5) = 0. \\]\nThis gives us two solutions: \\( b = 0 \\) or \\( b = 5 \\). Since \\( b \\) is a base and must be greater than 1, we discard \\( b = 0 \\) and keep \\( b = 5 \\).\n\n","prefix_end":887,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,2331,17767,293,1124,8,323,279,15723,17767,393,1124,8,1741,429,279,46444,315,17767,393,880,1124,8,553,17767,393,880,1124,8,3059,304,17767,220,18,16,880,1124,568,1205,1414,429,17767,393,284,293,481,220,16,1124,3593,5338,11,1077,594,3158,17767,393,880,1124,8,323,17767,220,18,16,880,1124,8,304,2331,220,16,15,13,576,1372,17767,393,880,1124,8,304,2331,220,16,15,374,17767,393,1124,701,323,279,1372,17767,220,18,16,880,1124,8,304,2331,220,16,15,374,17767,220,18,65,488,220,16,1124,568,15277,11,582,614,279,23606,510,78045,393,1124,15136,393,284,220,18,65,488,220,16,13,1124,921,12549,17767,393,284,293,481,220,16,1124,701,582,27679,17767,393,1124,8,448,17767,293,481,220,16,1124,982,78045,320,65,481,220,16,29776,17,284,220,18,65,488,220,16,13,1124,921,8033,25591,323,15491,7766,279,23606,11